 Magnite, Inc. was formerly known as The Rubicon Project, Inc. and changed name to Magnite, Inc. in July 2020. The company was incorporated in 2007 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael G. Barrett | CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 971 people. Revenue per employee of $735K ranks in the above the sector median among Communication Services peers, improving at 17%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $171K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $79K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Magnite, Inc. is a mid-cap communication services business with a $3.9B market cap on $714M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +2.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -5% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $166M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 23 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.63\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.2%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 46% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4559875038115603},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Communication Services ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Magnite (NASDAQ:MGNI) Stock: Insider Sean Patrick Buckley Sells 10,991 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/magnite-nasdaqmgni-stock-insider-sean-patrick-buckley-sells-10991-shares.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794003766.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.91,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Magnite (MGNI) Following Its Q3 Earnings Beat And Raised Outlook Has Valuation Back In Focus","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywal